@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+<div class="flex flex-column gap txt-align-start pad-inline" style="--row-gap: 0.5em">
+  <strong>Posting as a bot</strong>
+  <p class="margin-none">Send the message as the body of a <code>POST</code> request. The room ID is the number at the end of the room’s address, and the bot must be in that room.</p>
+  <pre class="margin-none"><code>curl -d "Deploy finished ✅" <%= room_bot_messages_url("ROOM_ID", "BOT_CODE") %></code></pre>
+  <p class="margin-none">To post a file, send it as <code>attachment</code>: <code>curl -F "attachment=@report.png" …</code></p>
+
+  <strong>Answering mentions</strong>
+  <p class="margin-none">When someone mentions a bot that has a webhook URL, Campfire sends the message to it as JSON in a <code>POST</code> request. To reply right away, respond with <code>200</code> and a <code>text/plain</code> or <code>text/html</code> body. To reply later (or not at all), respond with <code>204</code>, and post to the <code>room.reply_to</code> path from the request when you’re ready.</p>
+
+  <strong>Saying hello</strong>
+  <p class="margin-none">When a bot is added to a room, Campfire sends its webhook URL a <code>joined</code> event with the room. Reply the same way as to a mention to post into that room.</p>
+
+  <strong>Limits</strong>
+  <p class="margin-none">A bot can post up to <%= User::RateLimited::POSTS_LIMIT %> messages in any <%= User::RateLimited::POSTS_PERIOD.inspect %>, replies to its webhook included. The next one is turned away with <code>429</code>, and the bot has to wait <%= User::RateLimited::COOLDOWN.inspect %> (see the <code>Retry-After</code> header). A bot that keeps trying while it waits, or whose webhook fails <%= Webhook::MAX_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES %> times in a row, is suspended until an administrator reactivates it.</p>
+</div>
